14
00:54:46,956 --> 00:54:52,956
Hawking is a 2004 biographical drama television film directed
by Philip Martin and written by Peter Moffat.

15
00:58:41,739 --> 00:58:47,739
Starring Benedict Cumberbatch, it chronicles Stephen Hawking's early years as a PhD student at the University of
Cambridge, following his search for the beginning of time, and his struggle against motor neurons disease.

16
01:02:36,521 --> 01:02:42,521
It premiered in the UK in April 2004.

17
01:06:31,304 --> 01:06:37,304
The film received positive reviews, with critics particularly
lauding Cumberbatch's performance as Hawking.

18
01:10:26,086 --> 01:10:32,086
It received two British Academy Television Awards nominations:
Best Single Drama and Best Actor (Cumberbatch).

19
01:14:20,869 --> 01:14:26,869
Cumberbatch won the Golden Nymph for Best Performance
by an Actor in a TV Film or Miniseries.

20
01:18:15,652 --> 01:18:21,652
Cumberbatch's portrayal of Hawking was the first portrayal
of the physicist on screen not by himself.

21
01:22:10,434 --> 01:22:16,434
The film explores themes of physics, biography, scientist, 1960s, phd thesis.

22
01:26:05,217 --> 01:26:11,217
The tone is emotional.
